xf86drm: give ACPI-enumerated platform devices a unique bus identity

drmParseOFBusInfo() falls back to MODALIAS when a platform device has no
OF_FULLNAME, then takes the substring after the last ':'.

That fallback breaks for ACPI-enumerated platform devices. An ACPI modalias
is terminated with ':' -- for example:

    /sys/dev/char/226:0/device/uevent:MODALIAS=acpi:CIXH5010:

so strrchr(name, ':') finds the *trailing* colon and the resulting bus name
is the empty string. Every ACPI platform DRM device therefore ends up with
an identical (empty) drmPlatformBusInfo.

drmDevicesEqual() compares platform devices with memcmp() over that struct,
so all such devices compare equal, and the de-duplication pass in
drmGetDevices2() folds them into a single drmDevice. Only the first device
survives enumeration; the rest become invisible to userspace.

Even ignoring the trailing colon, MODALIAS is the wrong key here: it encodes
the ACPI hardware ID, which is shared by every instance of the same device
type, so sibling instances would still collide.

On a CIX Sky1 board (ARM64, ACPI boot) this is easy to observe. The board has
three linlondp display devices and a panthor GPU:

    $ ls /dev/dri/
    card0  card1  card2  card3  renderD128  renderD129  renderD130  renderD131

but drmGetDevices2() reports one:

    drmGetDevices2 -> 1 device(s)
      dev[0] bustype=2 nodes=0x5 fullname="" /dev/dri/card0 /dev/dri/renderD128

Because the GPU is not enumerated, Mesa reports "MESA-LOADER: failed to
retrieve device information" and falls back to software rendering, panvk
reports "Failed to detect any valid GPUs in the current config", and wlroots
fails with "Failed to get DRM device: No such device" -- so a compositor
never advertises zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 and every client is software-only, on a
board with a perfectly functional GPU.

Use the sysfs device name instead when OF data is absent. The kernel already
makes it unique per device instance (e.g. "CIXH5010:00", "CIXH5010:01"), and
the primary and render nodes of one device share it -- exactly the identity
semantics drmDevicesEqual() needs. With this change:

    drmGetDevices2 -> 3 device(s)
      dev[0] bustype=2 nodes=0x5 fullname="CIXH5010:04" /dev/dri/card2 /dev/dri/renderD130
      dev[1] bustype=2 nodes=0x5 fullname="CIXH5010:01" /dev/dri/card1 /dev/dri/renderD129
      dev[2] bustype=2 nodes=0x5 fullname="CIXH5010:00" /dev/dri/card0 /dev/dri/renderD128

Devices that do expose OF_FULLNAME are unaffected; only the no-OF fallback
path changes.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>

---
 xf86drm.c | verified against libdrm 2.4.134 on CIX Sky1 (Orion O6N)

--- a/xf86drm.c	2026-08-04 14:40:22.065985410 -0400
+++ b/xf86drm.c	2026-08-04 14:40:22.106903688 -0400
@@ -4293,24 +4293,32 @@
 static int drmParseOFBusInfo(int maj, int min, char *fullname)
 {
 #ifdef __linux__
-    char path[PATH_MAX + 1], *name, *tmp_name;
+    char path[PATH_MAX + 1], real[PATH_MAX + 1], *name, *tmp_name;
 
     snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "/sys/dev/char/%d:%d/device", maj, min);
 
     name = sysfs_uevent_get(path, "OF_FULLNAME");
     tmp_name = name;
     if (!name) {
-        /* If the device lacks OF data, pick the MODALIAS info */
-        name = sysfs_uevent_get(path, "MODALIAS");
-        if (!name)
-            return -ENOENT;
+        /*
+         * The device lacks OF data -- typically an ACPI-enumerated platform
+         * device. Do not fall back to MODALIAS here: an ACPI modalias has a
+         * trailing ':' (e.g. "acpi:CIXH5010:"), so stripping to the last ':'
+         * yields an empty name, and it is shared by every instance of the
+         * same HID regardless. Either way drmDevicesEqual() would compare
+         * distinct devices as equal and drmGetDevices2() would fold them
+         * into one.
+         *
+         * Use the sysfs device name instead (e.g. "CIXH5010:00"). It is
+         * unique per device instance, and the primary and render nodes of
+         * one device share it -- exactly the identity semantics required.
+         */
+        if (!realpath(path, real))
+            return -errno;
 
-        /* .. and strip the MODALIAS=[platform,usb...]: part. */
-        tmp_name = strrchr(name, ':');
-        if (!tmp_name) {
-            free(name);
+        tmp_name = strrchr(real, '/');
+        if (!tmp_name)
             return -ENOENT;
-        }
         tmp_name++;
     }
 
